---
import LessonLayout from '../../../layouts/LessonLayout.astro';
---
<LessonLayout title="Workbook &mdash; The Eucharist" cic="CCC 1322-1419" scripture="">

<section class="content">

<h2>Student Workbook</h2>
<p class="big-question">For use after class or in groups.</p>

<h3>Remembering the Essentials</h3>

<ol>
<li>What does the word "Eucharist" mean?</li>
<li>Why is the Eucharist called the "source and summit of the Christian life"?</li>
<li>What is "transubstantiation"?</li>
<li>What is the difference between "remembering" Jesus and making Him "present" in the Mass?</li>
<li>What did Jesus say in John 6 about His flesh and blood?</li>
</ol>

</section>

<section class="content">

<h3>For Reflection and Writing</h3>

<div class="question-block">
<p class="question-block__q">1. When was the last time the Mass was for you truly an encounter with Christ, not just an obligation?</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
</div>

<div class="question-block">
<p class="question-block__q">2. Jesus says that without the Eucharist we have no life within us. Do you feel you need it?</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
</div>

<div class="question-block">
<p class="question-block__q">3. The senses do not perceive the real presence; faith does. What strengthens your faith in the Eucharist?</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
</div>

<div class="question-block">
<p class="question-block__q">4. If you knew Jesus is truly present in the Eucharist (and He is), what would change in your attitude at communion?</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
</div>

</section>

<section class="content">

<h3>Scripture to Memorize</h3>

<div class="bible-passage">
<p>"I am the living bread that came down from heaven; whoever eats of this bread will live forever."</p>
<p class="bible-passage__ref">&mdash; John 6:51</p>
</div>

</section>

<section class="content">

<hr />
